Hi Phil,
  Thanks for the run down and the link to SimDesign <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/SimDesign/vignettes/SimDesign-intro.html#24_Interpreting_the_results> which has most of these functions. I agree that it has excellent features, including the tibble output for passing to GGplot for plotting much of what is needed. I can recommend this approach for anyone wishing to go down this line.

Several people have reached out with ideas and codes for simulation analysis (thanks). These involve extracting particular parameters from each simulated participant (e.g., items administered, parameter estimates, etc) and combining them into a tibble for plotting or calculating correlations/error. Everything is already nicely in the mirt object so the desired parameters can be extracted through loops.

I found SimDesign <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/SimDesign/vignettes/SimDesign-intro.html#24_Interpreting_the_results> could do most things, with the custom code from the mirt object doing the rest :)

With Kind Regards,
    Conal

